<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tughshada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/739">739</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tughshada was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhar-khudah">Bukhar Khudah</a>, the local ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>, in the early 8th century. After the Arab general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutayba-ibn-muslim">Qutayba ibn Muslim</a> took Bukhara in 709 he installed the young Tughshada as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> prince. He reigned for about thirty years under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a>, outwardly accepting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, and was killed in 739 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>. His descendants kept the title under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>.</p></div>
